# Keep this secret stable for persistent sessions.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# Local browser GUI is on 3010; coordinator API on 3011 (avoids production on 3000/3001).
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3011
SWEAT_GUI_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3010
SWEAT_COORDINATOR_PORT=3011
SWEAT_SANDBOX_PROVIDER=smolvm
# Boots the people who get no repository checkout. Only read under smolvm.
SWEAT_CONTAINER_PROVIDER=docker
VITE_SWEAT_API_URL=http://localhost:3011

# Optional integrations and overrides
# LINEAR_MCP_API_KEY=

# Fine-grained PAT. See docs/github-token.md.
# SWEAT_GITHUB_REPOSITORY=owner/repository
# SWEAT_GITHUB_BASE=main
# SWEAT_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Required to grant the agent pull-request publishing.
# SWEAT_VERIFY_COMMAND=
# Local tags; `make dev` / `make agent` build these for your machine's arch.
SWEAT_AGENT_IMAGE=sweat-agent:latest
# Optional Cursor agent runtime image (Node 22.13+ / @cursor/sdk).
# SWEAT_CURSOR_AGENT_IMAGE=sweat-agent-cursor:latest
# Production/server hosts can point at the published images instead:
# SWEAT_AGENT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/4ug-aug/colony-agent:latest
# SWEAT_CURSOR_AGENT_IMAGE=ghcr.io/4ug-aug/colony-agent-cursor:latest

# CA bundle installed inside agent sandboxes, container or microVM. Required for
# an internal HTTPS endpoint -- a .local model gateway cannot hold a public cert.
# SWEAT_AGENT_CA_CERT=/absolute/path/to/company-ca.pem
# Resolver for agent sandboxes. A microVM guest otherwise uses 8.8.8.8 and
# 1.1.1.1, and Docker hands a container the same pair whenever the host resolves
# through a stub -- an internal zone is NXDOMAIN either way. Name a server that
# knows yours; a systemd-resolved stub (127.0.0.53) is not one, it is the
# sandbox's own loopback there -- take the upstream `resolvectl status` reports.
# Exactly one IP: smolvm's --dns takes no list, so a host with several resolvers
# picks one and loses the rest as failover.
# SWEAT_SANDBOX_DNS=10.0.0.53
# SWEAT_SANDBOX_MEM_MIB=4096
# SWEAT_SANDBOX_CPUS=2
# CA bundle the coordinator itself trusts, for connections behind an internal
# CA (self-hosted Outline, Linear through a TLS-inspecting proxy). Without it,
# those upstreams fail with UNABLE_TO_VERIFY_LEAF_SIGNATURE. On Linux,
# `make service-install` hoists this into the systemd unit Environment=.
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/absolute/path/to/company-ca.pem
# Where a sandbox guest reaches the coordinator, overriding what the sandbox
# itself reports. Leave it unset unless you know better: a smolvm guest reaches
# the host on its own loopback (TSI redirects it), and a container resolves
# host.container.internal. Rootless Docker is the exception -- give it the host's
# LAN address, or run `make setup` to install the host-loopback drop-in.
# SWEAT_MCP_HOST=http://192.168.1.47
